From: Locietta <loia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: btf: don't emit BTF layout section for Docker Desktop

Since Linux 7.1, pahole >= 1.31 is asked to encode the BTF layout
section. Its offset and length are stored in the layout_off/layout_len
fields appended to struct btf_header, which are then non-zero for
vmlinux and module BTF.

Docker Desktop (seen on 4.80 and 4.93) embeds a cilium/ebpf older than
v0.22, which treats header bytes past the 24 it knows about as padding
that must be zero. Loading its oom tracer and mutagen selfowner objects
then fails with:

  parsing .BTF header: header padding: encountered non-zero byte

and Docker Desktop refuses to start.

Stop requesting the layout section. pahole still writes the 32-byte
header, but layout_off/layout_len stay zero, which older parsers accept.
The section only helps tools parse BTF kinds they don't know about, so
nothing in the WSL setup depends on it. Drop this once Docker ships
cilium/ebpf v0.22 or newer.

Link: https://github.com/Locietta/xanmod-kernel-WSL2/issues/174
---
 scripts/Makefile.btf | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/Makefile.btf b/scripts/Makefile.btf
index e66e13e79..3de432d88 100644
--- a/scripts/Makefile.btf
+++ b/scripts/Makefile.btf
@@ -18,7 +18,9 @@ pahole-flags-$(call test-ge, $(pahole-ver), 126)  = -j$(JOBS) --btf_features=enc
 
 pahole-flags-$(call test-ge, $(pahole-ver), 130) += --btf_features=attributes
 
-pahole-flags-$(call test-ge, $(pahole-ver), 131) += --btf_features=layout
+# Docker Desktop's eBPF loaders (cilium/ebpf < v0.22) reject non-zero
+# layout fields in the BTF header, so don't emit the layout section.
+# pahole-flags-$(call test-ge, $(pahole-ver), 131) += --btf_features=layout
 
 endif
 
-- 
2.55.0
